			<div class="content" id="post-content-3808520">
									

<p>So the core idea here is pretty good - an old god trying to use social media to become popular/worshipped again and being utterly clueless at it - but I have a few problems with the article.</p>
<p>For starters, it just feels kind of bloated - lots of extraneous detail on the specific social media managers and its company. I feel like you could trim this down a lot without losing anything. It could also use another editing pass; you've also got a few missing words or weird word choices, especially early on in the article (I didn't make a list, sorry).</p>
<p>My other issue is how they are dealing with this thing in the first place. They think its some kind of god, but based on what? Besides the documents they got from the agency, they don't seem to have any source of knowledge for what it is, and don't seem to make any effort to actually find it and put it into containment - surely this agency representing it would have its address or something? You say its a god and then treat it as if its some purely digital entity that can't be contained.</p>
<p>As I said, I think you've got a decent idea here, but I think it still needs some work.</p>

							</div>

								
